course: dictionary
lesson: 11311
title: Words for almost-colours
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some colours are not quite one colour. Adding -ish to a colour word means "a bit like" or "a little". So yellowish means a little yellow, or partly yellow.
explain: «The old paper had gone yellowish at the edges.» The paper is not bright yellow. It has only a little yellow in it, so the word tells you how much.
explain: Look for the -ish ending in other colours too: greenish, reddish and bluish all work the same way. Try the test: take off the -ish, then ask, "Is it a little of that colour?"
fact: The ending -ish means "a bit like" or "somewhat".
fact: «Yellowish» means a little yellow, or partly yellow.
fact: The Sun looks yellowish from the ground, because our air scatters blue light. From space, the Sun looks white.
fact: Blood is a yellowish liquid called plasma. It carries red cells, white cells and platelets.
fact: Artists, scientists and doctors use words like yellowish to describe colours more exactly than just "yellow".
exercise: «The Sun looks yellowish from the ground.» What does yellowish mean? | Dark blue | Completely white | *A little yellow | Bright red
exercise: Blood is a yellowish liquid. What is the name of the liquid part of blood? | *Plasma | Water | Milk | Sap
exercise: Find the word that means a little yellow in this sentence: «The leaves turned yellowish when the plant had no water.» | water | leaves | plant | *yellowish
test: Which word means partly yellow? | *Yellowish | Bright red | Pure white | Dark blue
test: Adding -ish to a colour word usually means | the opposite colour | a much brighter colour | a brand-new colour with no name | *a bit like that colour
exam: The leopard «matched the 'sclusively yellowish-greyish-brownish colour of the High Veldt to one hair». What does yellowish-greyish-brownish show about that colour? | Just one plain colour | Pure bright red | The blue of the sky at night | *A mix of yellow, grey and brown
